  "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)\u2248f(a,b)+\u2207f(a,b)\\cdot \u27e8x-a,y-b\u27e9.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & \u2248f(2,1)+\u2207f(2,1)\\cdot \u27e8x-2,y-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =f(2,1)+\u27e8{f}_{x}(2,1),{f}_{y}(2,1)\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-2,y-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =2+\u27e8-1,-1\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-2,y-1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.98,0.94)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.98$ and $y=0.94,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.98,0.94) & \u22482+\u27e8-1,-1\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81.98-2,0.94-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =2+\u27e8-1,-1\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-0.02,-0.06\u27e9 \\\\  & =2+(-1)(-0.02)+(-1)(-0.06) \\\\  & =2+0.02+0.06 \\\\  & =2.08\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
